      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Capitol_Hill%2C_Calgary",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The Capitol Hill Cottage School, built in 1912, is one of only four surviving cottage‑type schools in Calgary.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        2
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.heritageinspiresyyc.org/heritage-places/communities-capitol-hill/",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Capitol Hill Park, created between 1932 and 1941, once hosted a playground, skating rinks, and a baseball field.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        26
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.heritageinspiresyyc.org/heritage-places/communities-capitol-hill/",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Annexed in 1910, the community saw most of its development after World War II.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        23
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.heritageinspiresyyc.org/heritage-places/communities-capitol-hill/",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "Capitol Hill Elementary and Pius Bilingual Elementary schools serve the neighbourhood’s residents.",
